Note = {8th International Congress of Engineering Physics, Merida, MEXICO, NOV
   07-11, 2016},
Abstract = {Wireless communications have experienced a tremendous development during
   the last decade. The interaction of the electromagnetic waves as a
   function of the frequency and intensity with physical objects remains
   largely unknown. This poses the challenge to study the physical
   mechanisms involved to actually quantify the impact of the interaction
   with other objects caused by various electromagnetic waves-emitting
   sources. Here, we proposed the design of a plane SRR (Split-Ring
   Resonator) with metamaterial circular rings for S-Band frequency range.
   To guide the construction of the SRR prototype, simulations of the
   bandwidth were conducted using the Finite Integral technique. A
   logarithmic function describes the dependence of the simulated resonant
   frequency. The maximum simulated bandwidth of the SRR can be reached
   with an even number of concentric rings.},
