Note = {IEEE International Autumn Meeting on Power, Electronics and Computing
   (ROPEC), Ixtapa, MEXICO, NOV 08-10, 2017},
Organization = {IEEE; IEEE CENTRO OCCIDENTE SECT},
Abstract = {The Mexican Sign Language (MSL) has its own structure and grammar
   different from the Spanish spoken in Mexico. The MSL is composed of more
   than 1000 signs used by the deaf community of this country. Few hearing
   people know and use MSL, therefore there is a communication barrier
   between hearing and deaf people. In order to overcome this issue, we
   propose a non-invasive sign detection application, so that the
   interlocutor interacts with the system in a natural way interpreting a
   set of signs of the MSL using a bimodal cognitive vision system. Our
   application uses a Kinect sensor to obtain the gestures, geometric
   moments and Hidden Markov models to process it. From experiments
   performed with 10 people, it was concluded that our application achieved
   an average sensitivity of 86\% and an average specificity of 80\%.},
