Note = {International Workshop on Advanced Computational and Experimental
   Techniques in Nonlinear Dynamics, Cusco, PERU, AUG, 2015},
Abstract = {We investigate the motion of a massless body interacting with the
   Maxwell relative equilibrium, which consists of n bodies of equal mass
   at the vertices of a regular polygon that rotates around a central mass.
   The massless body has three equilibrium a{''}<currency> (n) -orbits from
   which families of Lyapunov orbits emerge. Numerical continuation of
   these families using a boundary value formulation is used to construct
   the bifurcation diagram for the case n = 7, also including some
   secondary and tertiary bifurcating families. We observe
   symmetry-breaking bifurcations in this system, as well as certain
   period-doubling bifurcations.},
