Pages = {1957-1962},
Month = {OCT},
Abstract = {The epileptic state, or status epilepticus (SE), is the most serious
   situation manifested by individuals with epilepsy, and SE events can
   lead to neuronal damage. An understanding of the molecular, biochemical
   and physiopathological mechanisms involved in this type of neurological
   disease will enable the identification of specific central targets,
   through which novel agents may act and be useful as SE therapies.
   Currently, studies have focused on the association between oxidative
   stress and SE, the most severe epileptic condition. A number of these
   studies have suggested the use of antioxidant compounds as alternative
   therapies or adjuvant treatments for the epileptic state.},
