   and Yarkoni, Tal},
Title = {How open science helps researchers succeed},
Journal = {ELIFE},
Year = {2016},
Volume = {5},
Month = {JUL 7},
Abstract = {Open access, open data, open source and other open scholarship practices
   are growing in popularity and necessity. However, widespread adoption of
   these practices has not yet been achieved. One reason is that
   researchers are uncertain about how sharing their work will affect their
   careers. We review literature demonstrating that open research is
   associated with increases in citations, media attention, potential
   collaborators, job opportunities and funding opportunities. These
   findings are evidence that open research practices bring significant
   benefits to researchers relative to more traditional closed practices.},
