Pages = {357-369},
Month = {MAY},
Abstract = {In this article the concept of immaterial labor is dialectically related
   to the cycle of material labor in the production and reproduction of
   capital and bourgeois society. The article reflects on how this affects
   the dynamics of social classes and their struggles in contemporary
   capitalist society. Immaterial labor, like its manual counterpart, is
   also subject to capitalism's essential contradictions as well as its
   processes and tendencies. Various authors, including Latin American
   Marxists, are drawn upon to explore further this historical process.},
